arguments:
file
option
options and file arguments can be intermixed arbitrarily. later options override earlier options that are incompatible
no option => list the contents of directories not recursively and omitting files with names beginning with .
for other non option arg, list just the file names
if no non option arg specified, operate on c_dir acting as if "ls ."
default => sorted alphabetically according to the locale settings in effet, if stdout is a terminal, output is in columns (sorted vertically) and control characters are output as questions mark; otherwise output listed one per line and control char output as-is
exit status: 
	0 success
	1 minor problems (failure to access a file or directory not specified as a command line argument. Happend when listing a dir in which entries are actively being removed or renamed)
	2 serious trouble (e.g., memory exhausted, invalid option, failure to acces a file or dir specified as a command line argument or a dir loop)